    [2198] = "Search for the original creator of the shattered necklace to learn of its potential value.",
    [2199] = "Bring five silver bars to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.",
    [2200] = "Search for clues as to the current disposition of Talvash's necklace within Uldaman.  The slain paladin he mentioned was the person who has it last.",
    [2201] = "Find the ruby, sapphire, and topaz that are scattered throughout Uldaman.  Once acquired, contact Talvash del Kissel remotely by using the Phial of Scrying he previously gave you.$B$BFrom the journal, you know...$B* The ruby has been stashed in a barricaded Shadowforge area.$B* The topaz has been hidden in an urn in one of the Trogg areas, near some Alliance dwarves.$B$B* The sapphire has been claimed by Grimlok, the trogg leader.",
    [2202] = "Bring 12 Magenta Fungus Caps to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath.",
    [2204] = "Obtain a power source from the most powerful construct you can find in Uldaman, and deliver it to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.",
    [2240] = "Read Baelog's Journal, explore the hidden chamber, then report to Prospector Stormpike.",
    [2278] = "Speak with stone watcher and learn what ancient lore it keeps.  Once you have learned what lore it has to offer, activate the Discs of Norgannon.",
    [2279] = "Take the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the Explorers' League in Ironforge.",
    [2280] = "Take the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the one of the sages in Thunder Bluff.",
    [2283] = "Look for a valuable necklace within the Uldaman dig site and bring it back to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar.  The necklace may be damaged.",
    [2284] = "Find a clue as to the gems' whereabouts in the depths of Uldaman.",
    [2318] = "Find someone who can translate the paladin's journal.  The closest location that might have someone is Kargath, in the Badlands.",
    [2338] = "Let Jarkal borrow the necklace.  In exchange, he will translate the journal for you.",
    [2339] = "Recover all three gems and a power source for the necklace from Uldaman, and then bring them to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath.  Jarkal believes a power source might be found on the strongest construct present in Uldaman.$B$BFrom the journal, you know...$B* The ruby has been stashed in a barricaded Shadowforge area.$B* The topaz has been hidden in an urn in one of the Trogg areas, near some Alliance dwarves.$B* The sapphire has been claimed by Grimlok, the trogg leader.",
    [2340] = "Deliver the Necklace and Gem Salvage to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar.",
    [2341] = "Visit Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath to see if he was successful.",
    [2342] = "Get Patrick Garrett's family treasure from their family chest in the South Common Hall of Uldaman, and bring it to him in the Undercity.",
    [2359] = "Steal the Defias Tower Key, break into the Defias Tower and uncover the contents of the Duskwood Chest. Take whatever information you find back to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind. Read Kearnen's Journal to gain insight about the tower.\n",
    [2360] = "Travel to Westfall and find Agent Kearnen for your debriefing.",
    [2361] = "I gladly give you this necklace, mighty $C.  You have done me an invaluable service, and for that I thank you.  Wear it with pride, and make sure you mention loudly and repeatedly who made it for you!$B$BAlso, if you could toss in the fact that it really isn't cursed, that would be great.",
    [2398] = "Find Baelog in Uldaman.",
    [2418] = "Bring 8 Dentrium Power Stones and 8 An'Alleum Power Stones to Rigglefuzz in the Badlands.",
    [2439] = "Take your reward voucher to Dinita Stonemantle in the Vault of Ironforge.",
    [2440] = "Take the reward voucher to Bena Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff.",
    [2458] = "Travel to the Venture Co. Tower, north of the Sludge Fen and contact the Shattered Hand's covert operative, Taskmaster Fizzule.$B$BWhen the tower is in sight, use the Flare Gun to signal your arrival to Taskmaster Fizzule. Fire off TWO flares, then approach Taskmaster Fizzule and perform the Shattered /Salute.$B$BThese actions must be performed in the correct order, as Fizzule will attack and terminate any person he does not recognize.",
    [2460] = "Perform the Shattered Salute on Shenthul.",
    [2478] = "Steal Silixiz's Tower Key from Foreman Silixiz, then kill two Mutated Venture Co. Drones, two Venture Co. Patrollers, and two Venture Co. Lookouts.$B$BAssassinate Grand Foreman Gallywix and take his head, then pick the lock on Gallywix's lockbox and steal the Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture. Take the Cache and Gallywix's Head back to Shenthul in Orgrimmar for further instruction.\n",
    [2479] = "Travel to Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills and deliver the Sample of Zanzil's Mixture to Serge Hinott.$B$BTo get to Tarren Mill, take the Zeppelin to the Undercity and follow the road south through Silverpine and towards Hillsbrad. Follow the signs!\n\n",
    [2480] = "Wait for Serge Hinott to complete the cure.",
    [2607] = "Speak with Doc Mixilpixil in the cellar of the Barracks.",
    [2608] = "/Lay down to be examined by Doc Mixilpixil. How can he find the cure if he can't find the cause?",
    [2609] = "Bring Doc Mixilpixil one bundle of Simple Wildflowers, one Leaded Vial, one Bronze Tube, and one Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread. The 'itis' doesn't cure itself, young $g fella:lady;. ",
